{"id":"98720726b7d85150178b8ee33c901664106e2f75","axis":"silent","repo":"traefik/traefik","sha":"98720726b7d85150178b8ee33c901664106e2f75","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","lines":["@@ -77,6 +77,8 @@ Prefer modern standard-library packages (`slices`, `maps`, `cmp`, ...) over hand"," "," - **Logging.** The project uses `github.com/rs/zerolog` exclusively — do not import `log`, `slog`, or `logrus`. Inside a middleware, get a logger via `middlewares.GetLogger(ctx, name, typeName)` (see [`pkg/middlewares/middleware.go`](./pkg/middlewares/middleware.go)) where `typeName` is a package-level `const` like `const typeNameForward = \"ForwardAuth\"`. Elsewhere, extract the logger from the context with `log.Ctx(ctx)` and attach it to a new context with `.WithContext(ctx)`."," - **Context propagation.** `context.Context` is always the first argument, named `ctx`. Avoid `context.Background()` in request paths; propagate from the caller. Define custom context keys as unexported struct types (`type myKey struct{}`) to prevent collisions.","+- **ResponseWriter wrappers implement `Unwrap`.** Any type wrapping an `http.ResponseWriter` must expose it with `Unwrap() http.ResponseWriter`. `http.ResponseController` walks the chain through `Unwrap` to reach the connection (read/write deadlines, full duplex, ...); a wrapper without it breaks the chain for every handler below it, and the failure is silent (`http.ErrNotSupported`). Do not add `Flush`/`Hijack` methods that only forward to the wrapped writer, do not implement the deprecated `http.CloseNotifier` (use `req.Context().Done()`), and do not assert `http.Flusher`/`http.Hijacker` on a ResponseWriter: call `http.NewResponseController(rw).Flush()`/`.Hijack()`, and return its error as is (callers check it with `errors.Is(err, http.ErrNotSupported)`). A wrapper that must act on flush or hijack implements `FlushError() error` or `Hijack()` and calls the wrapped writer through `http.ResponseController`. A wrapper that holds back the status code (retry, failover, error pages) must not flush before writing it: flushing commits an implicit `200`.","+- **Third-party handlers are used directly, plugins are wrapped.** A library must flush and hijack through `http.ResponseController` and give the next handler a writer with `Unwrap`; if it does not, fix it upstream. Yaegi/WASM plugins, whose code is unknown, may assert `http.Flusher`/`http.Hijacker` on the writer they receive and may give the next handler a writer without `Unwrap`, which is their right (e.g. a buffering writer must not be flushed past). The plugin builders wrap them with `wrapExternal` (or `wrapExternalWith` when the build function also returns a value), see [`pkg/plugins/external.go`](./pkg/plugins/external.go): deadlines, full duplex and hijacking fall back to the writer given to the plugin when the plugin's writer does not support them; flushing never falls back."," "," ## Testing conventions"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"go.mod","lines":["@@ -39,7 +39,8 @@ require ("," \tgithub.com/huandu/xstrings v1.5.0"," \tgithub.com/influxdata/influxdb-client-go/v2 v2.7.0"," \tgithub.com/influxdata/influxdb1-client v0.0.0-20200827194710-b269163b24ab // No tag on the repo.","-\tgithub.com/klauspost/compress v1.19.2","+\t// TODO: pin a released version once https://github.com/klauspost/compress/pull/1272 is part of a release.","+\tgithub.com/klauspost/compress v1.20.4-0.20261021124103-35c6f98a5cb9"," \tgithub.com/kvtools/consul v1.0.2"," \tgithub.com/kvtools/etcdv3 v1.0.3"," \tgithub.com/kvtools/redis v1.2.1"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"go.sum","lines":["@@ -776,8 +776,8 @@ github.com/kisielk/errcheck v1.5.0/go.mod h1:pFxgyoBC7bSaBwPgfKdkLd5X25qrDl4LWUI"," github.com/kisielk/gotool v1.0.0/go.mod h1:XhKaO+MFFWcvkIS/tQcRk01m1F5IRFswLeQ+oQHNcck="," github.com/klauspost/compress v1.13.4/go.mod h1:8dP1Hq4DHOhN9w426knH3Rhby4rFm6D8eO+e+Dq5Gzg="," github.com/klauspost/compress v1.13.6/go.mod h1:/